<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for ad-hoc signed fork builds.

  The App Sandbox cannot be used with an ad-hoc signature. secinitd never
  answers the sandbox-initialisation XPC request, so the process deadlocks in
  _libsecinit_appsandbox during dyld's initialisers — before AppKit is even
  loaded. It presents as a live PID with one thread that never opens a window.
  Sandboxing needs a real signing identity (a Team ID and provisioning
  profile), which a locally or CI built fork does not have.

  So com.apple.security.app-sandbox is omitted here, along with the two
  temporary-exception mach-lookup entries, which only mean anything inside the
  sandbox.

  Consequence: an unsandboxed Maccy stores its history at
  ~/Library/Application Support/Maccy rather than inside
  ~/Library/Containers/org.p0deje.Maccy. script/install-artifact.sh migrates
  the data across on first install.

  Maccy/Maccy.entitlements remains upstream's, unmodified, for real signed builds.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
